      "message": "Carlos:\n\nHave you run a full set of tests / AI analysis on this?\n\nI find it hard to believe such a bug would be present in 6.1/6.6 which has been out on phones (pixel 6-9/10) and other devices for years and years...\n\nI simply don\u0027t recall there being (m)any bug reports pre-6.12...\n\nI *do* see the quoted \u0027fixes\u0027 commit is in 6.1... but are we sure that\u0027s not some sort of mis-attribution on the fixing commit?\n\nThat original commit is also just a oneliner that claims:\n\nxfrm6: release dev before returning error\n\nWe forget to call dev_put() on error path in xfrm6_fill_dst(),\nits caller doesn\u0027t handle this.\n\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/84c4a9dfbf430861e7588d95ae3ff61535dca351%5E%21/",
