      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T21:55:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here\u0027s what jetski (from a 7.3-rc7 checkout) says:\n\n\u003e please analyze commit 136992de9bb91871084ae52d172610541c76e4d2 - is the fixes tag correct - or is the bug introduced elsewhere (is it correct to backport this to 6.1 and 6.6 or should this be only in 6.12)\n\n### Summary                                                                                                      \n                                                                                                                   \n  • Is the Fixes: tag correct? Yes. Fixes: 84c4a9dfbf43 (\"xfrm6: release dev before returning error\") (v3.10-rc2)  \n  is accurate — that commit is what introduced the double dev_put() / netdev_put().                                \n  • Should this be backported to 6.1 and 6.6, or only 6.12? It is correct (and necessary) to backport to 6.1 and 6.\n  6 as well as 6.12. The bug affects all of them identically, and upstream stable already has backports            \n  queued/merged for 6.1 (97e032e5733e4), 6.6 (df6856c2dda91), and 6.12 (43de8a49335e6).                            \n  ──────                                                                                                           \n  ### 1. Bug Mechanics                                                                                             \n                                                                                                                   \n  In xfrm6_fill_dst():                                                                                             \n                                                                                                                   \n    static int xfrm6_fill_dst(struct xfrm_dst *xdst, struct net_device *dev,                                       \n                  const struct flowi *fl)                                                                             \n        \n    {                                                                                                              \n        struct rt6_info *rt \u003d dst_rt6_info(xdst-\u003eroute);                                                             \n                                                                                                                   \n        xdst-\u003eu.dst.dev \u003d dev;                                                                                       \n        netdev_hold(dev, \u0026xdst-\u003eu.dst.dev_tracker, GFP_ATOMIC);                                                      \n                                                                                                                   \n        xdst-\u003eu.rt6.rt6i_idev \u003d in6_dev_get(dev);                                                                    \n        if (!xdst-\u003eu.rt6.rt6i_idev) {                                                                                \n            netdev_put(dev, \u0026xdst-\u003eu.dst.dev_tracker);                                                                    \n            xdst-\u003eu.dst.dev \u003d NULL; /* \u003c-- added by 136992de9bb9 */                                                       \n            return -ENODEV;\n  \n        }                                                                                                            \n                                                                                                                   \n  xfrm6_fill_dst() is called via xfrm_fill_dst() from two places in xfrm_policy.c:                                 \n                                                                                                                   \n  1. xfrm_bundle_create(): on error, jumps to free_dst: and calls dst_release_immediate(\u0026xdst0-\u003eu.dst).            \n  2. xfrm_create_dummy_bundle(): on error, jumps to free_dst: and calls dst_release(dst1).                         \n                                                                                                                   \n  Both error paths invoke dst_destroy(), which unconditionally executes:                                           \n                                                                                                                   \n    netdev_put(dst-\u003edev, \u0026dst-\u003edev_tracker);                                                                       \n                                                                                                                   \n  Because netdev_put() is only a no-op when dst-\u003edev is NULL, leaving xdst-\u003eu.dst.dev \u003d dev after calling          \n  netdev_put() in xfrm6_fill_dst() causes dst_destroy() to release the same net_device reference and dev_tracker a \n  second time.                                                                                                     \n  ──────                                                                                                           \n  ### 2. Why Fixes: 84c4a9dfbf43 Is Correct                                                                        \n                                                                                                                   \n  1. Before 84c4a9dfbf43 (v2.6.25 – v3.9):                                                                         \n  When xfrm6_fill_dst() was created in 25ee3286dcbc ([IPSEC]: Merge common code into xfrm_bundle_create, v2.6.25-  \n  rc1), it did:                                                                                                    \n    xdst-\u003eu.dst.dev \u003d dev;                                                                                         \n    dev_hold(dev);                                                                                                 \n                                                                                                                   \n    xdst-\u003eu.rt6.rt6i_idev \u003d in6_dev_get(rt-\u003eu.dst.dev);                                                            \n    if (!xdst-\u003eu.rt6.rt6i_idev)                                                                                    \n        return -ENODEV;\nWhen xfrm_bundle_create() hit goto free_dst, it called dst_free(dst0) → dst_destroy(dst0) (since dst0-\u003e__refcnt  \n  was 0 and dst0-\u003eobsolete was DST_OBSOLETE_FORCE_CHK (-1), i.e. not \u003e 0). dst_destroy() did if (dst-\u003edev)         \n  dev_put(dst-\u003edev);, properly releasing the dev_hold(dev) reference once.                                         \n  2. Introduction of the bug in 84c4a9dfbf43 (v3.10-rc2, May 2013):                                                \n  Commit 84c4a9dfbf43 (xfrm6: release dev before returning error) assumed the caller did not clean up dst-\u003edev and \n  added dev_put(dev) to the !xdst-\u003eu.rt6.rt6i_idev error path without setting xdst-\u003eu.dst.dev \u003d NULL. Because xdst-\n  \u003eu.dst.dev was already set to dev, this immediately caused a double dev_put(dev) when xfrm_bundle_create() called\n  dst_free(dst0) → dst_destroy().                                                                                  \n  (Note: The second caller, xfrm_create_dummy_bundle(), added in a0073fe18e71 in v3.9-rc1, originally had a broken \n  dst_release(dst1) on a 0-refcount dst that leaked dst1; once 52df157f17e5 (\"xfrm: take refcnt of dst when        \n  creating struct xfrm_dst bundle\", v4.13-rc1) initialized xdst with initial_ref \u003d 1, both callers\u0027 error paths    \n  reached dst_destroy() and triggered the double put.)                                                             \n  3. Conversion to ref_tracker in 4177e4960594f (v5.16-rc5, Dec 2021):                                             \n  When Eric Dumazet converted xfrm6_fill_dst() to dev_hold_track() / dev_put_track() in 4177e4960594f (xfrm: use   \n  net device refcount tracker helpers), he explicitly called out this bug in the commit message:                   \n  │ Error path in xfrm6_fill_dst() releases the reference, but does not clear xdst-\u003eu.dst.dev, so I wonder if this \n  │ could lead to double dev_put() in some cases, where a dst_release() _is_ called by the callers in their error  \n  │ path.                                                                                                          \n  │ This extra dev_put() was added in commit 84c4a9dfbf430 (\"xfrm6: release dev before returning error\")           \n                                                                                                                   \n  ──────                                                                                                           \n  ### 3. Backporting to 6.1 and 6.6 vs. 6.12                                                                       \n                                                                                                                   \n  Backporting 136992de9bb9 to 6.1 and 6.6 (in addition to 6.12) is completely valid and necessary:                 \n                                                                                                                   \n  • Identical ownership \u0026 teardown flow: In 6.1, 6.6, and 6.12, xfrm6_fill_dst() uses netdev_hold() / netdev_put(),\n  xfrm_bundle_create() calls dst_release_immediate(\u0026xdst0-\u003eu.dst) on error, xfrm_create_dummy_bundle() calls       \n  dst_release(dst1) on error, and dst_destroy() calls netdev_put(dst-\u003edev, \u0026dst-\u003edev_tracker).\n  • xfrm6_dst_destroy() is safe on early failure across all three trees:                                           \n      • xdst-\u003eu.rt6.rt6i_idev is NULL, which is guarded by if (likely(xdst-\u003eu.rt6.rt6i_idev)).                     \n      • rt6_uncached_list_del(\u0026xdst-\u003eu.rt6) is not yet added to the uncached list when xfrm6_fill_dst() fails      \n      early:                                                                                                       \n          • In 6.1, xfrm6_dst_destroy() checks if (xdst-\u003eu.rt6.rt6i_uncached_list) before calling                  \n          rt6_uncached_list_del(), which is NULL thanks to memset_after(xdst, 0, u.dst) in xfrm_alloc_dst().       \n          • In 6.6 and 6.12 (after d288a162dd1c and 418a73074da9), dst_init() initializes INIT_LIST_HEAD(\u0026dst-     \n          \u003ert_uncached), so rt6_uncached_list_del() sees list_empty(\u0026rt-\u003edst.rt_uncached) and does nothing.",
      "parentUuid": "12961d18_3f0ce927",
      "revId": "06aabb3c55412104814644e8d1b37df04940d99a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
