      "message": "\u003e is this needed even on the *latest* 6.1/6.6/6.12/6.18 LTS or has it been fixed already (if so, which ones)\n\nIt has already been backported and merged into all four of those LTS trees (linux-6.1.y, linux-6.6.y, linux-     \n  6.12.y, and linux-6.18.y):                                                                                       \n                                                                                                                   \n   LTS Branch         │ Backport Commit    │ First Included In  │ Latest Release on Branch  │ Status on Latest LTS\n  ────────────────────┼────────────────────┼────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────\n   6.1.y              │ 97e032e5733e4      │ v6.1.183           │ v6.1.189 (a500ba24937a9)  │ Already fixed\n   6.6.y              │ df6856c2dda91      │ v6.6.148           │ v6.6.158 (a91a6aa9253c6)  │ Already fixed\n   6.12.y             │ 43de8a49335e6      │ v6.12.101          │ v6.12.112 (7aba70ab2e8d8) │ Already fixed\n   6.18.y             │ ff636d7b7cba6      │ v6.18.42           │ v6.18.56 (17ad2612c11a7)  │ Already fixed\n                                                                                                                   \n  (For completeness, it was also backported to 7.1.y in e078da1b4e113 / v7.1.6, and landed mainline in v7.2-rc4 via\n  389704eb516b0.)                                                                                                  \n                                                                                                                   \n  So if you are on the latest point release of 6.1, 6.6, 6.12, or 6.18, the fix in xfrm6_policy.c:88-93 is already \n  present and no further backport is needed.",
